>
>GDSM would help for AC but I have MR two ways now and three ways post
>Quest.  I really want SDSM which is why I mention fountain dipping.  I
>don't see much risk, especially with my pet nearby.  GDSM is tougher to
>steal since the cloak needs to come off first.

  The way to get SDSM for a wizard is a 20k sacrifest while getting to
XL 30 by dallying with foocubi.  Get Cha to max by magic trap dancing.
If you're chaotic same race sacrifice will summon peaceful major demons.
Some of those will be foocubi.  Dally until you're XL 30 and then keep
going.  You'll still get HP and Mana boosts. 

  A chaotic human wizard with an altar near the Ft Ludios level (or just
above the Castle. (Yes, it can happen)) can lead self-portable
sacrifices to the altar, then buc the loot.  (Barracks are also good
sources.)  Many foocubi will result.


  Eventually a silver dragon will show up.  Don't kill it unless you
have wand/spell of turn undead.  Keep reviving it until you get scales.
If you run out of charges, leave it alive until you get the spell.
Write the spell if you have to.


>
>I'm concerned about going deeper without more intrinsics.  I remember
>sacing some elves that I really should have used for SleepR.  Looking
>at what can get generated at DL10-16, I'm a bit spooked to be honest.
>I'm prepared enough that - with care - it's a pretty safe decent I
>guess.

  Be careful.  Right now your big concern is to get the Eye.  That means
getting to XL 14.  That probably means foocubi dancing.  That means
maximizing your charisma.  That means b!oGA and magic trap dancing.
(You didn't think playing a wizard would be easy, did you?)

  Get your strength up and get dagger skill to Expert.  That's a deadly
weapon and at range.  Learn to conserve it for dangerous monsters.
Elbereth as necessary.  Learn which monsters don't respect Elbereth.
Spell of magic missile is good, but does damage based on XL.  At XL 10
it does 6d6 damage.  That averages to 21 points of damage per hit per
monster.

>
>Note teleportitis is mostly moot since I can ^T already since lvl 8.
>For other classes it's lvl12.  That is why =oTC would be great.

  You'll get TC at XL 17.  

  A sacrifest where you concentrate on improving stats and XL will get
you everything you need.  As your XL goes up tougher monsters will be
generated (either randomly or through the spell of create monster.)
Tougher monsters will help your XL, especially once you start generating
foocubi.  

  You don't have to kill foocubi of the wrong gender.  Eventually an
amulet of change can make them useful.  The spell/wand of locking can
give you a private altar room.

  Even now, patience and the spell of create monster can let you
sacrifest until you're XL 14.  Don't forget that monsters will be
generated randomly.  Use telepathy to check.  Lead them to the altar
while waiting for mana to regenerate.  Again, higher XL will generate
tougher monsters which are better sacrifices.

  Using daggers is important to conserve mana.  Using thrown daggers is
important since Magicbane will scare/confuse monsters, making it more
difficult to kill the uncarryable monsters on the altar.

  It takes a some effort and patience at first, but if you work on all
the factors things improve exponentially.  You have what you need to get
what you need.  Do you have the patience to use them properly?


